# LF everywhere, for every text file. This tree is edited from both Windows and
# WSL over /mnt/x. Windows git and the WSL global config both run
# core.autocrlf=true, which warns on every add that LF "will be replaced by
# CRLF". eol=lf beats autocrlf on both platforms, so the working copy and the
# index stay LF and the warning stops. Same rule as backgammondb/.gitattributes.
# text=auto lets git decide what is text, so an unlisted binary is still safe.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Markdown stays LF so planning docs diff cleanly against the other repos'
# copies (see chalkstream.dev/docs/planning-standards.md § 5). Redundant under
# the catch-all, kept because it states the reason.
*.md text eol=lf
